{
 "en": [
  {
   "title": "Overview",
   "icon": "industrialfurnace:furnace_controller",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "Molten Industry adds the Industrial Furnace, a 3×3×3 RF-powered multiblock. It smelts 8 identical items per batch, twice as fast as a vanilla furnace, and works with every smelting recipe, modded ones included."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Blocks"
    },
    {
     "items": [
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_controller",
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_casing",
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_energy_port",
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_input_bus",
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_output_bus",
      "industrialfurnace:furnace_fluid_port"
     ]
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Controller",
       "Front of the furnace. Right-click it to see status, energy and progress."
      ],
      [
       "Casing",
       "The walls."
      ],
      [
       "Energy Port",
       "Accepts RF from cables."
      ],
      [
       "Input Bus",
       "9 slots for things to smelt."
      ],
      [
       "Output Bus",
       "9 slots for the results."
      ],
      [
       "Fluid and Gas Port",
       "Optional. A fluid tank and a Mekanism gas tank, 16,000 mB each. Filled by pipes or a bucket; right-click shows the contents. Used by the infuser (water for concrete) and the compressor (osmium gas)."
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Building",
   "icon": "industrialfurnace:furnace_casing",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "1. Build a 3×3×3 cube with a hollow centre."
    },
    {
     "text": "2. Put the controller in the middle of one wall, facing outwards."
    },
    {
     "text": "3. Fill the other walls with casing. Anywhere in the walls, replace casing with at least one Energy Port, one Input Bus and one Output Bus."
    },
    {
     "text": "4. Right-click the controller: §aFurnace formed§r means it is ready."
    },
    {
     "heading": "You need"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Controller",
       "1"
      ],
      [
       "Casing",
       "22"
      ],
      [
       "Energy Port",
       "1"
      ],
      [
       "Input Bus",
       "1"
      ],
      [
       "Output Bus",
       "1"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "More ports are fine; you then need fewer casings."
    },
    {
     "heading": "The formed furnace"
    },
    {
     "text": "Once formed, the blocks turn into one 3D machine model with a firebox, a chimney and hatches where the ports are. Break any block and it falls apart into regular blocks again."
    },
    {
     "text": "With EMI, the Industrial Furnace Structure page shows a rotating model. Click it to view the furnace layer by layer."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Running it",
   "icon": "minecraft:iron_ingot",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Per batch",
       "8 identical items"
      ],
      [
       "Batch time",
       "half the vanilla cook time (5 s for ores), at least 1 s"
      ],
      [
       "Energy use",
       "40 RF/t (4,000 RF per batch of ores)"
      ],
      [
       "Buffer",
       "200,000 RF"
      ],
      [
       "Max input",
       "10,000 RF/t"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Buses"
    },
    {
     "text": "The Input Bus pulls smeltable items from adjacent chests and inventories, 16 every half second, and leaves everything else alone."
    },
    {
     "text": "The Output Bus pushes results into adjacent chests, barrels and pipes. Pipes and hoppers can also work with the buses directly."
    },
    {
     "text": "If the output buses are full, the furnace waits and keeps the finished batch until there is room."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Signs of work"
    },
    {
     "text": "While smelting, flames burn behind the grate and the furnace hums. It does not grant smelting XP."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Crusher",
   "icon": "industrialfurnace:crusher_controller",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "The Industrial Crusher is built like the furnace: a 3×3×3 cube with a hollow centre and the same casing, buses and energy port, but with a Crusher Controller."
    },
    {
     "items": [
      "industrialfurnace:crusher_controller"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Once formed it turns into one 3D model with an intake hopper, two toothed rollers behind a window and a brass gear on the side. The rollers and gear spin while it works."
    },
    {
     "heading": "What it crushes"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Ores",
       "doubled: iron, gold, diamond, emerald, coal and quartz ore give 2; copper gives 6 raw copper; lapis 10; redstone 8"
      ],
      [
       "Stone",
       "stone → cobblestone → gravel → sand"
      ],
      [
       "Gravel",
       "sand plus a 10% chance of flint"
      ],
      [
       "Other",
       "sandstone → 4 sand, glowstone → 4 dust, bone → 6 bone meal, blaze rod → 4 powder"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Other mods"
    },
    {
     "text": "These recipes appear by themselves, only when the mod is installed:"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Mekanism",
       "osmium, tin, lead, uranium ore → 2 raw; fluorite → 6 gems"
      ],
      [
       "Thermal",
       "silver, nickel ore → 2 raw; ruby, sapphire → 2; tin and lead when Mekanism is absent"
      ],
      [
       "AE2",
       "certus quartz, fluix, sky stone → dust; ender pearl → ender dust"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The furnace smelts every mod's smelting recipes, e.g. Mekanism and Thermal dusts into ingots. The energy port takes RF from any mod's cables, and the buses work with Mekanism and Thermal pipes and AE2 interfaces."
    },
    {
     "text": "Other ores work if a recipe targets their Forge tag (forge:ores/...). Change recipes with a datapack or KubeJS: type industrialfurnace:crushing."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Running it"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Per batch",
       "up to 8 identical items"
      ],
      [
       "Batch time",
       "5 s (stone, bones and the like: 3 s)"
      ],
      [
       "Energy use",
       "60 RF/t"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The buses work as on the furnace: the input bus pulls only crushable items from adjacent chests, the output bus pushes the results out."
    },
    {
     "recipe": "industrialfurnace:crusher_controller"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Infuser",
   "icon": "industrialfurnace:infuser_controller",
